stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 750 Td (# SROW Public Reference Comparison Source \(v0.1\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 720 Td (## Chapter 1: Introduction to Structured Resolution-Oriented Writing) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 690 Td (Structured Resolution-Oriented Writing \(SROW\) is a communication protocol for making structured knowledge readable and navigable by both humans and machines.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 660 Td (Structure is a form of reader respect. Explicit structural hierarchy reduces cognitive friction for both human readers and automated inference agents.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 630 Td (Progressive disclosure is a staged presentation that exposes orientation and structure before deeper analytical explanation or granular assertion records.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 600 Td (## Chapter 2: Technical Architecture and Stable Identity) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 570 Td (The stable-ID algorithm uses SHA-256 truncated to 16 hexadecimal characters over the canonical lexically sorted source-block binding key.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 540 Td (Structured Resolution-Oriented Writing \(SROW\) establishes explicit structural compliance for software and AI validation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 510 Td (## Chapter 3: Boundaries and Limitations) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 480 Td (SROW is an expression and structuring protocol, not a cognition architecture or internal thought representation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 450 Td (Structured records improve inspectability and retrieval precision; they do not guarantee factual truth or eliminate model error.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 420 Td (This public reference material contains only authorized public companion samples and does not include the complete manuscript or governed meaning-unit database.) Tj ET
endstream
